# RULES: ERROR HANDLING

## Role

Define how errors flow through the system.

## What to fill in during synthesis

- return type/pattern for operations with errors;
- where the error is caught and how it is presented to the user;
- error states per boundary (loading/empty/error/permission);
- prohibitions (e.g. leaking internal detail, stacktraces, or sensitive payloads into logs).

## Typical triggers

- operation returning an error result;
- error flow, retry, or failure feedback.
